From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 81/81] PC5: a wait on an event or a semaphore spins briefly before
 it sleeps (Wine patch 0998)

A game that hands many small jobs to worker threads sets their events
thousands of times a frame. A worker asleep on its event makes each set
go through Wine's server and wake it, several microseconds each on the
console. A worker now checks its event for up to 100 microseconds before
it sleeps (WINE_PS5_SYNC_SPIN_US, 0 off): a set in that time takes the
fast path and nothing has to be woken.
